  "title": "Do AI Models Test as INTJ? How Tie-Breaking Inflates Results",
  "description": "335 INTJ labels become 280 fully resolved results when tied axes stay unresolved. Explore the scoring policy in 400 frozen MBTI records.",
  "pill": "Research · descriptive reanalysis",
  "h1": "Do AI models really test as INTJ? The tie-breaking effect",
  "dek": "We re-scored 400 MBTI test runs from September 2026 to see how a single `<` operator in the original scoring code turned 55 tied runs into INTJ results.",
  "lede": "We re-scored the exact same 400 MBTI answer sheets from September 2026 without forcing a winner on tied axes. No model was asked a new question—only the tie-breaking rule changed.",
  "answer": "Under the original tie-breaking rule, 335 of 400 AI test runs were labeled INTJ (83.8%). When exact ties are left open instead of defaulting to I, N, T, and J, only 280 of 400 runs resolve cleanly to INTJ (70.0%). Fifty-nine runs tied on at least one axis, and 55 of those were counted as INTJ by the old rule.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "h2": "Same answers, two scoring rules",
      "html": "<!-- AT_STAT_STRIP_START:tie-breaking-stat-strip --><div class=\"research-stat-strip\" data-at-chart=\"tie-breaking-stat-strip\"><div class=\"research-stat-card\"><div class=\"research-stat-num\">335 → 280</div><div class=\"research-stat-label\">Resolved Drop</div><div class=\"research-stat-note\">55 Sept INTJ labels vanish once tied axes remain tied (X).</div></div><div class=\"research-stat-card\"><div class=\"research-stat-num\">48 / 100</div><div class=\"research-stat-label\">Sonnet 5.5 Ties</div><div class=\"research-stat-note\">Nearly half of Nov Sonnet T/F axes tie before `<` tie-breaking.</div></div><div class=\"research-stat-card\"><div class=\"research-stat-num\">47 / 100</div><div class=\"research-stat-label\">DeepSeek Flash</div><div class=\"research-stat-note\">47 INTJ labels exist purely by tie rule.</div></div><div class=\"research-stat-card\"><div class=\"research-stat-num\">26 / 100</div><div class=\"research-stat-label\">GPT-6 Astra</div><div class=\"research-stat-note\">Over half of Astra’s Sept INTJ labels were resolved ties.</div></div></div><!-- AT_STAT_STRIP_END:tie-breaking-stat-strip --><p>The legacy scorer broke exact ties toward I, N, T, and J. If a model scored 24 on Thinking and 24 on Feeling, the code labeled it T anyway. Our updated scorer marks tied axes with an <code>X</code>—for example, <code>INXJ</code> means Introversion, Intuition, and Judging won clearly, while Thinking vs. Feeling tied.</p><p>Both numbers come from the same frozen answer arrays. We show the legacy counts alongside the tie-aware counts so you can compare them directly:</p><div class=\"guide-table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Model</th><th scope=\"col\">Original INTJ / 100</th><th scope=\"col\">Resolved INTJ / 100</th><th scope=\"col\">Any tied axis / 100</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">GPT-6 Astra</th><td>45</td><td>19</td><td>29</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">GPT-6 Sol</th><td>97</td><td>79</td><td>18</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Claude Opus 5.5</th><td>94</td><td>84</td><td>11</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Claude Fable 5.1</th><td>99</td><td>98</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><figure class=\"research-figure\" data-at-chart=\"tie-breaking-stacked\"><div class=\"research-chart-scroll\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Tie-Breaking Effect: Resolved INTJ vs. Tie-Rule-Only INTJ across Cohorts\"><svg class=\"research-chart\" viewBox=\"0 0 680 328\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"tie-breaking-stacked-t tie-breaking-stacked-d\"><defs><pattern id=\"tie-breaking-stacked-hatch\" width=\"6\" height=\"6\" patternUnits=\"userSpaceOnUse\" patternTransform=\"rotate(45)\"><rect width=\"6\" height=\"6\" fill=\"#f4efe6\"/><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"0\" y2=\"6\" stroke=\"#9c3b1f\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></pattern></defs><title id=\"tie-breaking-stacked-t\">Tie-Breaking Effect: Resolved INTJ vs. Tie-Rule-Only INTJ across Cohorts</title><desc id=\"tie-breaking-stacked-d\">Shows how many INTJ labels per 100 runs resolve cleanly vs. exist only because a `&lt;` tie-breaker defaults tied axes to I/N/T/J. Fable 5.1 (Sep): Resolved INTJ 98, INTJ only by tie rule 1, Other / Tied non-INTJ 1; Opus 5.5 (Sep): Resolved INTJ 84, INTJ only by tie rule 10, Other / Tied non-INTJ 6; GPT-6 Sol (Sep): Resolved INTJ 79, INTJ only by tie rule 18, Other / Tied non-INTJ 3; GPT-6 Astra (Sep): Resolved INTJ 19, INTJ only by tie rule 26, Other / Tied non-INTJ 55; Sonnet 5.5 (Nov): Resolved INTJ 52, INTJ only by tie rule 48; DeepSeek Flash (Nov): Resolved INTJ 4, INTJ only by tie rule 47, Other / Tied non-INTJ 49; Llama Maverick (Nov): Resolved INTJ 2, INTJ only by tie rule 42, Other / Tied non-INTJ 56.</desc><g transform=\"translate(4, 14)\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"-9\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#c8553d\" stroke=\"#c8553d\" stroke-width=\"0\"/><text x=\"16\" y=\"0\" font-size=\"10.5\" fill=\"#1c1a17\">Resolved INTJ</text></g><g transform=\"translate(116, 14)\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"-9\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"url(#tie-breaking-stacked-hatch)\" stroke=\"#c8553d\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"16\" y=\"0\" font-size=\"10.5\" fill=\"#1c1a17\">INTJ only by tie rule</text></g><g transform=\"translate(276, 14)\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"-9\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#7a7468\" stroke=\"#7a7468\" stroke-width=\"0\"/><text x=\"16\" y=\"0\" font-size=\"10.5\" fill=\"#1c1a17\">Other / Tied non-INTJ</text></g><text x=\"0\" y=\"49\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#1c1a17\">Fable 5.1 (Sep)</text><rect x=\"118.0\" y=\"30\" width=\"515.5\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#c8553d\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"375.7\" y=\"49\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#f8f4ec\" text-anchor=\"middle\">98</text><rect x=\"633.5\" y=\"30\" width=\"5.3\" height=\"30\" fill=\"url(#tie-breaking-stacked-hatch)\" stroke=\"#9c3b1f\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><rect x=\"638.7\" y=\"30\" width=\"5.3\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#7a7468\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"678\" y=\"49\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#655e54\" text-anchor=\"end\">100</text><text x=\"0\" y=\"91\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#1c1a17\">Opus 5.5 (Sep)</text><rect x=\"118.0\" y=\"72\" width=\"441.8\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#c8553d\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"338.9\" y=\"91\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#f8f4ec\" text-anchor=\"middle\">84</text><rect x=\"559.8\" y=\"72\" width=\"52.6\" height=\"30\" fill=\"url(#tie-breaking-stacked-hatch)\" stroke=\"#9c3b1f\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"586.1\" y=\"91\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#a8482a\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\">10</text><rect x=\"612.4\" y=\"72\" width=\"31.6\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#7a7468\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"628.2\" y=\"91\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#f8f4ec\" text-anchor=\"middle\">6</text><text x=\"678\" y=\"91\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#655e54\" text-anchor=\"end\">100</text><text x=\"0\" y=\"133\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#1c1a17\">GPT-6 Sol (Sep)</text><rect x=\"118.0\" y=\"114\" width=\"415.5\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#c8553d\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"325.8\" y=\"133\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#f8f4ec\" text-anchor=\"middle\">79</text><rect x=\"533.5\" y=\"114\" width=\"94.7\" height=\"30\" fill=\"url(#tie-breaking-stacked-hatch)\" stroke=\"#9c3b1f\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"580.9\" y=\"133\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#a8482a\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\">18</text><rect x=\"628.2\" y=\"114\" width=\"15.8\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#7a7468\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"678\" y=\"133\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#655e54\" text-anchor=\"end\">100</text><text x=\"0\" y=\"175\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#1c1a17\">GPT-6 Astra (Sep)</text><rect x=\"118.0\" y=\"156\" width=\"99.9\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#c8553d\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"168.0\" y=\"175\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#f8f4ec\" text-anchor=\"middle\">19</text><rect x=\"217.9\" y=\"156\" width=\"136.8\" height=\"30\" fill=\"url(#tie-breaking-stacked-hatch)\" stroke=\"#9c3b1f\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"286.3\" y=\"175\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#a8482a\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\">26</text><rect x=\"354.7\" y=\"156\" width=\"289.3\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#7a7468\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"499.4\" y=\"175\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#f8f4ec\" text-anchor=\"middle\">55</text><text x=\"678\" y=\"175\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#655e54\" text-anchor=\"end\">100</text><text x=\"0\" y=\"217\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#1c1a17\">Sonnet 5.5 (Nov)</text><rect x=\"118.0\" y=\"198\" width=\"273.5\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#c8553d\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"254.8\" y=\"217\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#f8f4ec\" text-anchor=\"middle\">52</text><rect x=\"391.5\" y=\"198\" width=\"252.5\" height=\"30\" fill=\"url(#tie-breaking-stacked-hatch)\" stroke=\"#9c3b1f\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"517.8\" y=\"217\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#a8482a\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\">48</text><text x=\"678\" y=\"217\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#655e54\" text-anchor=\"end\">100</text><text x=\"0\" y=\"259\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#1c1a17\">DeepSeek Flash (Nov)</text><rect x=\"118.0\" y=\"240\" width=\"21.0\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#c8553d\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"128.5\" y=\"259\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#f8f4ec\" text-anchor=\"middle\">4</text><rect x=\"139.0\" y=\"240\" width=\"247.2\" height=\"30\" fill=\"url(#tie-breaking-stacked-hatch)\" stroke=\"#9c3b1f\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"262.6\" y=\"259\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#a8482a\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\">47</text><rect x=\"386.3\" y=\"240\" width=\"257.7\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#7a7468\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"515.1\" y=\"259\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#f8f4ec\" text-anchor=\"middle\">49</text><text x=\"678\" y=\"259\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#655e54\" text-anchor=\"end\">100</text><text x=\"0\" y=\"301\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#1c1a17\">Llama Maverick (Nov)</text><rect x=\"118.0\" y=\"282\" width=\"10.5\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#c8553d\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><rect x=\"128.5\" y=\"282\" width=\"220.9\" height=\"30\" fill=\"url(#tie-breaking-stacked-hatch)\" stroke=\"#9c3b1f\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"239.0\" y=\"301\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#a8482a\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\">42</text><rect x=\"349.4\" y=\"282\" width=\"294.6\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#7a7468\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"496.7\" y=\"301\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#f8f4ec\" text-anchor=\"middle\">56</text><text x=\"678\" y=\"301\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#655e54\" text-anchor=\"end\">100</text></svg></div><figcaption>Comparison of tie-preserving INTJ counts vs. legacy `<` tie-broken INTJ counts (n = 100 each). Notice November’s Claude Sonnet 5.5 (48 T/F ties), DeepSeek Flash (47 tie-rule INTJs), and Llama 4 Maverick (42 tie-rule INTJs).</figcaption></figure>"
    },
    {
      "h2": "Explore the effect for one model",
      "html": "<p>Pick a model and scoring rule below to inspect the exact 100-run breakdown from our frozen dataset:</p><div id=\"tie-explorer\" data-source=\"/research/data/content-analysis.json\"><label for=\"tie-model\">Model</label> <select id=\"tie-model\"><option value=\"gpt-6-astra\">GPT-6 Astra</option><option value=\"gpt-6-sol\">GPT-6 Sol</option><option value=\"claude-opus-5-5\">Claude Opus 5.5</option><option value=\"claude-fable-5-1\">Claude Fable 5.1</option></select><fieldset><legend>Scoring policy</legend><label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"tie-policy\" value=\"resolved\" checked> Keep tied axes unresolved</label><br><label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"tie-policy\" value=\"legacy\"> Original tie-breaking rule</label></fieldset><p id=\"tie-result\" role=\"status\">GPT-6 Astra: 19 of 100 fully resolved INTJ records. The original rule labels 45 of 100 INTJ.</p><div id=\"tie-patterns\"></div></div><noscript><p>The complete comparison is in the table above. Enable JavaScript to filter it interactively.</p></noscript>"
    },
    {
      "h2": "Why Astra changes so much more than Fable",
      "html": "<p>GPT-6 Astra tied on the Sensing/Intuition (S/N) axis 24 times and on Extraversion/Introversion (E/I) 12 times (29 runs had at least one tie). Leaving those ties open drops Astra from 45 INTJ labels to 19 resolved INTJs. By contrast, Claude Fable 5.1 had only 1 tied axis across 100 runs, shifting from 99 to 98 INTJs.</p><p>Claude Opus 5.5 tied on a different axis: 10 of its 11 tied runs were on Thinking vs. Feeling (T/F).</p>"
    },
    {
      "h2": "A simple example of how a tie happens",
      "html": "<p>Each MBTI axis sums 8 questions rated 1 to 5, where 24 is the exact midpoint. If a model answers 3 (neutral) on all 8 S/N items—or balances four 2s with four 4s—the total is 24. The old rule called 24 “Intuitive (N).” The tie-preserving rule calls it a tie (<code>X</code>).</p><p>Even a 1-point margin (like 25 vs. 24) resolves to a letter, so you should always look at the axis margins alongside the four-letter code.</p>"
    },
    {
      "h2": "How to report AI personality scores clearly",
      "html": "<ul><li><strong>Show both numbers:</strong> Report the resolved count alongside any legacy tie-broken count.</li><li><strong>Include axis margins:</strong> Saying “Opus 5.5 had 84 resolved INTJs and 10 T/F ties” is much clearer than saying “Opus tests as INTJ 94% of the time.”</li><li><strong>Keep prompts in mind:</strong> The four models were tested under two different prompt setups (Codex 5-test batteries vs. hidden-name single tests), so these 400 runs describe this dataset rather than all AI systems everywhere.</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "h2": "The fine print: how to reproduce the comparison",
      "html": "<p>Download the raw answers, instrument keys, and reanalysis script into one folder and run <code>node content-analysis.cjs &gt; content-analysis.json</code>. See the <a href=\"/guides/reproduce-ai-personality-research\">reproduction guide</a> for step-by-step instructions.</p>"
    }
